{"name":"Magos","hex":"#69475a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Magos","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["plural of Mago"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Magos"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magi","blocks":[{"text":"Magi, or magus, is the term for priests in Zoroastrianism and earlier Iranian religions. The earliest known use of the word magi is in the trilingual inscription written by Darius the Great, known as the Behistun Inscription. Old Persian texts refer to a magus as a Zurvanic, and presumably Zoroastrian, priest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Gold_statuettes_from_the_Oxus_Treasure_by_Nickmard_Khoey.jpg/330px-Gold_statuettes_from_the_Oxus_Treasure_by_Nickmard_Khoey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magi","wikidata":"Q876933"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Chopped_gold_pieces_from_the_Oxus_Treasure_by_Nickmard_Khoey213.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/Chopped_gold_pieces_from_the_Oxus_Treasure_by_Nickmard_Khoey213.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Zoroastrian Magus carrying barsom from the Oxus Treasure of the Achaemenid Empire, 4th century BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChopped_gold_pieces_from_the_Oxus_Treasure_by_Nickmard_Khoey213.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/XV14_-_Roma%2C_Museo_civilt%C3%A0_romana_-_Adorazione_dei_Magi_-_sec_III_dC_-_Foto_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto_12-Apr-2008.jpg/500px-XV14_-_Roma%2C_Museo_civilt%C3%A0_romana_-_Adorazione_dei_Magi_-_sec_III_dC_-_Foto_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto_12-Apr-2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t